      "topic": "Arithmetic",
      "answer": "b",
      "answer_source": "solutions_pdf:56.-SBI-Clerk-Prelims-2020-Quantitative-Aptitude-Solutions-.pdf",
      "answer_confidence": 0.87,
      "explanation": "Let 10 years ago, ages of Ram and Rahim were x years and 3x years, respectively. Then, present age of Ram = (x + 10) and present age of Rahim = (3x + 10) According to the question, x+10+5 3x+10+5 = ⇒ 3x + 45 = 6x + 30 ⇒ 3x = 15 ∴ x = 5 Hence, required ratio = 5+10 3×5+10 = 25 = 3 ∶5"
